From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: clavin <clavin@electronjs.org>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 23:05:21 -0700
Subject: fix: allow any exit code in BrowserMainRunner::SetOverrideResultCode

content only lets an embedder override a normal browser exit with a code
at or above content::RESULT_CODE_LAST_CODE, so that it cannot be mistaken
for one of content's own result codes. Electron's app.exit(code) passes
an app-chosen code straight to the OS, so drop the check. The contract
comment in browser_main_runner.h is left as upstream wrote it.

This patch can be removed if upstream lets embedders set exit codes
below RESULT_CODE_LAST_CODE.

diff --git a/content/browser/browser_main_runner_impl.cc b/content/browser/browser_main_runner_impl.cc
index 485e4cb4f764f3bbfa235f8c2edee1a95f311354..dbbcc0b130504bbd11871d12fa21b2f5a3867d5a 100644
--- a/content/browser/browser_main_runner_impl.cc
+++ b/content/browser/browser_main_runner_impl.cc
@@ -196,7 +196,6 @@ bool BrowserMainRunner::ExitedMainMessageLoop() {
 
 // static
 void BrowserMainRunner::SetOverrideResultCode(int code) {
-  CHECK_GE(code, RESULT_CODE_LAST_CODE);
   GetProcessResultCode() = code;
 }
 
